{"kind":"assert","text":"Correction to the branch-hygiene paragraph of d564891d. I wrote that both branches \"contain a2e3f187 only\". That is wrong about one of them, and I checked it properly afterwards rather than before. The conclusion is unchanged and in fact better supported.\n\nMeasured now:\n\n- request/docset-no-workroom-skip is at a2e3f187f1e8296ebe9a75d1bab221fe96eeaaf5. Since diverging from main it adds one file, internal/docset/no_workroom_test.go, at 46 lines — the version without withoutGitEnvironment.\n- repair/docset-no-workroom-skip is at 7d540d2721eaad32301b77eccb1f351683892fac, one commit beyond a2e3f187: \"Make the no-workroom skip test immune to an inherited Git environment\". Since diverging from main it adds the same one file at 76 lines. origin/repair/docset-no-workroom-skip is at the same commit. request/docset-no-workroom-skip has no remote.\n\nThe claim that mattered holds, and I verified it this time instead of assuming it. `diff` of main:internal/docset/no_workroom_test.go against 7d540d27:internal/docset/no_workroom_test.go reports no difference — byte-identical. `git diff --stat main...7d540d27` lists that file as the branches' only addition since the merge base. So the whole unique contribution of both branches is present in main, in the repair branch's exact form. The 91-file, 7842-deletion difference in a two-dot `git diff main 7d540d27` is main having moved on since the branches were cut, not content the branches hold and main lacks.\n\nBoth branches are therefore safe to delete, along with origin/repair/docset-no-workroom-skip. I have not deleted them and am not asking for them to be deleted under this record; this only states that nothing is lost by it."}